            "author": "japanese_kanta",
            "region": "JP",
            "shares": 0,
            "caption": "Practicing Japanese with AI feels easier than talking with a person. That's the catch. AI waits while you build your sentence. It stays on topic. People answer fast, change the subject, or ask something you didn't prepare for. Phrases for when the conversation moves too fast すみません、もう一度お願いします (sumimasen, mou ichido onegai shimasu) Sorry, one more time please. ちょっと待ってください (chotto matte kudasai) Please give me a second. 〜ということですか？ (... to iu koto desu ka?) Do you mean ...? Use AI to practice. Use people for the moments that matter. When did a real conversation go off script for you? Free Japan guide in my LINE. Link in my profile. #learnjapanese #businessjapanese #workinjapan #japaneseconversation",
